{"case_id":"T8020","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol","configuration","input semantics","serializer entry point"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["htmlCreatePushParserCtxt","htmlParseChunk","htmlDoRead","htmlCtxtReadMemory","htmlCreateDocParserCtxt","htmlCreateFileParserCtxt","htmlFindEncoding","htmlFindOutputEncoder","htmlDocDumpMemoryFormat","htmlSaveFileFormat"],"reason":"H0 exercises only a restricted HTML parsing/serialization configuration. Its pull call passes a NULL encoding to htmlReadMemory, and its push context passes no initial chunk and XML_CHAR_ENCODING_NONE to htmlCreatePushParserCtxt. This misses the changed explicit-encoding paths through xmlSwitchEncodingName and the changed ordering in htmlCreatePushParserCtxt where an initial chunk can be buffered before applying enc. Its push schedule is also fixed at 128-byte chunks, leaving boundary-sensitive htmlParseChunk state transitions underexplored. For output, H0 directly calls htmlDocContentDumpOutput with a NULL encoding on an unencoded output buffer, so it does not exercise the changed htmlFindOutputEncoder behavior or explicit/meta-derived encoding behavior in public dump/save APIs. These are material fuzz gaps because the diff changes encoding selection, progressive-parser stopping/state behavior, and encoded serialization/error handling.","evidence":["H0 calls htmlReadMemory(docBuffer, docSize, NULL, NULL, opts), so the encoding argument is always NULL despite changed explicit-encoding handling in htmlDoRead and related context constructors.","H0 calls htmlCreatePushParserCtxt(NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, XML_CHAR_ENCODING_NONE), so it never supplies constructor input and never selects a non-default enc; S1 buffers the initial chunk and then calls xmlSwitchEncoding(ctxt, enc).","H0 feeds htmlParseChunk using a constant maxChunkSize of 128, while S1 substantially changes htmlParseTryOrFinish and adds PARSER_STOPPED handling to htmlParseChunk.","H0 serializes with xmlAllocOutputBuffer(NULL) and htmlDocContentDumpOutput(out, doc, NULL), bypassing htmlFindOutputEncoder and the changed encoding-selection paths used by htmlDocDumpMemoryFormat, htmlNodeDumpFileFormat, htmlDocDump, htmlSaveFile, and htmlSaveFileFormat.","S1 changes htmlSaveFileFormat to derive the meta encoding from handler->name or UTF-8, a configuration-dependent behavior H0 never invokes."],"recommended_action":"Extend the harness with independently fuzzed modes for explicit pull encoding names, non-NONE push encodings, optional initial data in htmlCreatePushParserCtxt, and variable chunk schedules including splits around multibyte characters and markup delimiters. Add encoded serialization modes using htmlDocDumpMemoryFormat and an explicit-encoding save/dump API, with meta charset values derived from the fuzz input and allocation-failure limits retained."}
